    {
      "text": "Nicknamed “the bully of the sea,” Sharpedo is widely feared. Its cruel fangs grow back immediately if they snap off. Just one of these Pokémon can thoroughly tear apart a supertanker.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sharpedo can swim at speeds of up to 75 mph by jetting seawater out of its backside. This Pokémon’s drawback is its inability to swim long distances.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It pursues its prey at speeds of 75 mph and finishes them off with fangs that can crush iron. It is known as the bully of the sea.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has a sad history. In the past, its dorsal fin was a treasured foodstuff, so this Pokémon became a victim of overfishing.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "People believe that carrying one of its discarded fangs will prevent mishaps at sea, so the fangs are made into accessories.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It drinks in seawater and jets it from its rear to propel itself. It’s very sensitive to the scent of blood.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "As soon as it catches the scent of prey, Sharpedo will jet seawater from its backside, hurtling toward the target to attack at 75 mph.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is known as the Bully of the Sea. Any ship entering the waters Sharpedo calls home will be attacked—no exceptions.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
